1
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:12,387
Okay, good.

2
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:15,140
- It's better than making multiple trips.
- Right.

3
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:17,350
Nice, you're doing well.

4
00:00:18,059 --> 00:00:19,269
Watch your step.

5
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:21,062
STUMBLES

6
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:24,566
What is it?

7
00:00:25,608 --> 00:00:27,193
Darn it, I stepped on poop!

8
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:29,529
- You stepped on poop?
- I stepped on poop!

9
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:35,201
I really stepped on it

10
00:00:35,285 --> 00:00:36,327
You really did.

11
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:40,874
You didn't just step on it.
You rubbed it in, Zuha.

12
00:00:40,957 --> 00:00:44,210
What you stepped on
must've come from that cow.

13
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:45,378
Right, the rubbed-in poop.

14
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:51,593
BACK WITH TABLES AND CHAIRS FOR THE PARTY

15
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:52,510
Put them down.

16
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:53,845
Good job.

17
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:57,307
Hold on.

18
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:59,100
CHECKING

19
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:00,018
Is this poop?

20
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:00,935
CHECKING AGAIN

21
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:02,312
AND AGAIN

22
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:04,814
Is it there?
Isn't that poop on your shoes?

23
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:06,691
SHE SHAKES IT OFF OUTSIDE

24
00:01:06,775 --> 00:01:07,984
One, two, three.

25
00:01:08,777 --> 00:01:09,611
Okay.

26
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:12,906
You're really smelling it?

27
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:14,449
SHE SMELLS IT TO CHECK

28
00:01:14,532 --> 00:01:15,950
You did ballet for this?

29
00:01:17,744 --> 00:01:20,288
No, it's just in case.
But I think this is dirt.

30
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:22,082
But I think I can smell it.

31
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:25,668
- Kazuha stepped on poop on the way back.
- What?

32
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,713
No, I didn't.

33
00:01:30,673 --> 00:01:31,841
How do I prep these?

34
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:33,426
CHICKEN BREAST NAENGCHAE SALAD

35
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:35,011
I'll cut them into a size you want.

36
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:36,387
Cut them into long, thin strips.

37
00:01:36,471 --> 00:01:39,015
Peel the cucumbers
and remove the seeds.

38
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:40,141
"Long, thin strips."

39
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:42,185
- Yes, I'd appreciate that.
- Okay.

40
00:01:46,064 --> 00:01:47,273
You're pretty good.

41
00:01:47,982 --> 00:01:51,319
You're quite a good cook now.

42
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:52,278
Well, at home…

43
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:53,613
THE SOUS-CHEF CAN COOK A BIT

44
00:01:53,696 --> 00:01:54,989
I got sick of delivery food.

45
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:56,449
- Really?
- You don't cook?

46
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:57,992
I don't cook often.

47
00:01:58,076 --> 00:02:00,495
Since delivery apps
are set up so well in Korea,

48
00:02:00,578 --> 00:02:01,913
I don't end up cooking much.

49
00:02:01,996 --> 00:02:04,374
Hold on.
You said to cut them long and thin.

50
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:06,167
What? That's not it.

51
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:09,045
That's not how you cut them.

52
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:12,298
You have to julienne them
into long strips.

53
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:13,716
- Julienne them?
- Yeah.

54
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:14,634
They're sweet.

55
00:02:16,344 --> 00:02:19,180
CHOPPED INTO LITTLE PIECES

56
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:20,598
Hey, is this right?

57
00:02:20,682 --> 00:02:21,558
- What?
- This.

58
00:02:21,641 --> 00:02:23,893
No, you diced them.

59
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:26,104
I don't know how to julienne them.

60
00:02:26,604 --> 00:02:29,023
I don't know either,
so I asked you to do it, but you…

61
00:02:29,107 --> 00:02:31,276
Well, let's just do it this way.

62
00:02:31,359 --> 00:02:34,070
Shouldn't they be cut long like this?
I'm not good at cutting.

63
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:35,864
Aren't they supposed to look like this?

64
00:02:35,947 --> 00:02:38,616
And then, don't you chop them?

65
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,326
They're so thick. You'll lose a tooth.

66
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:42,328
How can we chew these?

67
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:43,413
Try one.

68
00:02:44,831 --> 00:02:45,790
THE BIZARRE CUTTING DUO

69
00:02:45,874 --> 00:02:47,167
They have to be crunchy though.

70
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:48,293
Make them a bit more…

71
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:50,086
What do you mean? Yours are thicker.

72
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:52,380
THICKLY SLICED AND DICED CARROTS

73
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:55,300
CHOPPED BELL PEPPERS

74
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:57,176
They're not coming out the way I wanted.

75
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,094
FLAT CUCUMBER PIECES

76
00:02:58,177 --> 00:02:59,429
This looks like feed for cows.

77
00:02:59,512 --> 00:03:01,598
THEY WERE SUPPOSED TO BE LONG AND THIN

78
00:03:02,181 --> 00:03:03,725
I'll try to make the dressing.

79
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:04,809
MAKING THE SALAD DRESSING

80
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:07,103
I have no idea how this will turn out.

81
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:09,439
I don't know the ratio.

82
00:03:12,358 --> 00:03:13,276
About this much.

83
00:03:13,359 --> 00:03:14,736
BY FEEL

84
00:03:15,445 --> 00:03:17,405
I didn't measure anything.
I just added them.

85
00:03:17,488 --> 00:03:19,240
- I don't measure either.
- You just do it.

86
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:20,450
SAME COOKING PHILOSOPHY

87
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:21,951
I went by feel.

88
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:23,453
We should taste-test it.

89
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:25,330
It's mustard-based.

90
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:26,706
- Mustard-based?
- Yeah.

91
00:03:26,789 --> 00:03:27,916
Isn't that a lot?

92
00:03:27,999 --> 00:03:29,208
SLURPING

93
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:31,628
FULL OF ANTICIPATION

94
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:38,092
You try it.

95
00:03:38,843 --> 00:03:39,677
It's not good?

96
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:42,639
It tastes like, "Do I have to eat this?"

97
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:48,394
Like, "Why?"

98
00:03:48,978 --> 00:03:51,731
"Why did they have to make salad?"
It tastes like that.

99
00:03:51,814 --> 00:03:53,691
THE REVIEW MAKES HER HUMBLE

100
00:03:53,775 --> 00:03:56,277
It's not that good. What am I missing?

101
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:03,159
SEARCHING AGAIN

102
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,662
Let's add sugar.

103
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:06,663
Sugar?

104
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:08,623
- I'll put it in.
- Okay.

105
00:04:12,293 --> 00:04:13,670
It needs to be sweet.

106
00:04:19,717 --> 00:04:21,302
NERVOUS

107
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:23,429
- It's much better.
- It's okay?

108
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:24,555
- Yeah.
- Much better?

109
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:25,556
Much better.

110
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:26,474
- It is?
- Yeah.

111
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:30,103
- Isn't it better?
- This is it.

112
00:04:31,187 --> 00:04:32,021
It's good.

113
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:33,815
I was worried about the dressing.

114
00:04:33,898 --> 00:04:35,608
- It's good.
- They'll eat this, right?

115
00:04:35,692 --> 00:04:36,943
- Yeah.
- It's not bad.

116
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:39,362
Salad takes a lot of work to make.

117
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:41,572
Shredding chicken breast takes so long.

118
00:04:41,656 --> 00:04:43,157
- I'll put it in.
- Okay.

119
00:04:43,241 --> 00:04:44,742
Put some in here too. Not all of it.

120
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:45,827
COMBINED

121
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:46,953
Time to mix it up.

122
00:04:47,036 --> 00:04:48,538
- Yeah.
- I think it'll be fine.

123
00:04:48,621 --> 00:04:49,622
It's good.

124
00:04:51,499 --> 00:04:53,876
How is it?
The dressing tastes good now, right?

125
00:04:56,337 --> 00:04:57,338
- It's good?
- Yeah.

126
00:04:58,172 --> 00:04:59,173
It's delicious.

127
00:04:59,257 --> 00:05:00,675
THE SALAD IS READY

128
00:05:00,758 --> 00:05:02,385
But today,

129
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:04,595
you're helping me more than I expected.

130
00:05:04,679 --> 00:05:05,805
Am I being helpful?

131
00:05:05,888 --> 00:05:07,223
I couldn't have done this alone.

132
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:08,141
RELIABLE

133
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:10,059
Three tables for now.

134
00:05:10,143 --> 00:05:11,477
THEY BEGIN ARRANGING TABLES BELOW

135
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:12,603
Okay.

136
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:14,647
I think we can use this as a table.

137
00:05:15,231 --> 00:05:16,607
- Right? Yeah.
- Like this?

138
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:18,776
- It's for the food.
- That's a great idea.

139
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:20,820
I think it'll work.

140
00:05:20,903 --> 00:05:23,197
I thought we were doing it like this.

141
00:05:23,281 --> 00:05:24,324
Hey, that's a good idea.

142
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:25,408
You're right.

143
00:05:25,491 --> 00:05:26,492
- Set it up.
- Good, right?

144
00:05:26,576 --> 00:05:28,703
- Set it up.
- They've never been used.

145
00:05:28,786 --> 00:05:29,620
TABLE FOR FOOD

146
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:30,538
It's nice.

147
00:05:30,621 --> 00:05:31,873
Let's make it flat.

148
00:05:32,665 --> 00:05:33,916
This way, the food won't spill.

149
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,668
MAKING IT FLAT WITH A TRAY

150
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:37,420
It's awkward to have the inside showing.

151
00:05:37,503 --> 00:05:38,546
LEAVING MUCH TO BE DESIRED

152
00:05:38,629 --> 00:05:39,756
Should we add another layer?

153
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:41,382
It'd be okay if we hid it.

154
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:42,425
Let's…

155
00:05:42,508 --> 00:05:43,885
LET'S COVER THE FRONT SIDE

156
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:47,013
Right.

157
00:05:47,096 --> 00:05:48,056
The lettuce.

158
00:05:48,139 --> 00:05:49,390
CABBAGE BLANKET APPEARS

159
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:50,475
Try covering the front.

160
00:05:50,558 --> 00:05:52,602
- It'll look great.
- Totally.

161
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:54,020
Hold this.

162
00:05:54,103 --> 00:05:55,438
LETTUCE TABLECLOTH

163
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:56,564
Great.

164
00:05:57,273 --> 00:05:58,441
It looks good.

165
00:06:00,193 --> 00:06:01,360
- It's Kian's B&B-esque.
- Yeah.

166
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:02,528
THIS IS KIAN'S B&B-ESQUE

167
00:06:02,612 --> 00:06:03,446
I think it's good.

168
00:06:03,529 --> 00:06:04,739
- Right?
- Yeah.

169
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:07,325
- Let's take what we brought…
- And unfold them?

170
00:06:07,408 --> 00:06:08,451
NOW TO PLACE ALL THE SEATS

171
00:06:08,534 --> 00:06:09,786
Let's wipe down the legs first.

172
00:06:09,869 --> 00:06:12,288
Boss, do we have any rags?

173
00:06:12,371 --> 00:06:13,372
- Rags?
- Yes.

174
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:14,332
RAGS TO CLEAN CHAIRS

175
00:06:14,415 --> 00:06:16,250
Use one of mine over there.

176
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:17,835
But this isn't a rag. It's a towel.

177
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:18,753
BOSS'S TOWELS

178
00:06:18,836 --> 00:06:20,713
I use towels as rags too.

179
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:22,423
What are you talking about?

180
00:06:25,635 --> 00:06:26,636
- What are you…
- Use it.

181
00:06:27,303 --> 00:06:29,180
- I can just wash it later.
- Seriously?

182
00:06:29,263 --> 00:06:31,265
- Yes.
- Then, I'm going to write on it.

183
00:06:31,349 --> 00:06:32,809
- "Rag."
- Go ahead.

184
00:06:32,892 --> 00:06:34,644
I use towels as rags and vice versa.

185
00:06:35,311 --> 00:06:36,479
You can just wash them.

186
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:38,648
He uses them as rags too?

187
00:06:38,731 --> 00:06:39,732
MARKED TO AVOID CONFUSION

188
00:06:39,816 --> 00:06:41,359
Write "rag" in Japanese for me.

189
00:06:41,442 --> 00:06:42,527
"Rag"?

190
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:43,611
- "<i>Sōkin</i>"?
- <i>Zōkin</i>.

191
00:06:43,694 --> 00:06:44,779
IN JAPANESE AS WELL

192
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:47,865
Gosh, this is…

193
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:51,911
That should do. Try setting one up.

194
00:06:51,994 --> 00:06:52,912
Wherever you like.

195
00:06:52,995 --> 00:06:53,871
Wherever I like?

196
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:55,039
Like an awards show.

197
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:57,291
- An awards show?
- Yeah.

198
00:06:57,875 --> 00:06:59,919
I think we'll need
big chairs in the front.

199
00:07:00,002 --> 00:07:00,837
AWARDS SHOW LAYOUT

200
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,547
Right in the front.

201
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,006
BIG CHAIRS IN THE FRONT

202
00:07:05,049 --> 00:07:06,467
4 PEOPLE PER TABLE

203
00:07:06,551 --> 00:07:08,469
There we go. Okay.

204
00:07:09,595 --> 00:07:10,429
Is this good?

205
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,140
Good job.

206
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:14,475
- Where should we put this?
- Let's put beverages…

207
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:16,144
- Okay.
- …and food on this.

208
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:17,603
Okay, food and beverages.

209
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:18,938
Okay. Good job.

210
00:07:19,021 --> 00:07:19,856
FOR REFRESHMENTS

211
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,441
It looks so good.

212
00:07:22,066 --> 00:07:22,900
That's done.

213
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:24,068
SATISFIED WITH THE LAYOUT

214
00:07:24,152 --> 00:07:26,195
Let's use these boxes then.

215
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:27,280
BOXES FOR DINING TABLES

216
00:07:27,363 --> 00:07:30,491
If we turn them over and cover them…

217
00:07:30,575 --> 00:07:31,701
- Right?
- There we go.

218
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:32,869
- It's a pizza.
- All set.

219
00:07:32,952 --> 00:07:33,953
That's good.

220
00:07:34,036 --> 00:07:35,037
PIZZA TABLE

221
00:07:35,121 --> 00:07:35,955
It looks great.

222
00:07:37,081 --> 00:07:38,666
- And an egg here.
- That looks good.

223
00:07:38,749 --> 00:07:39,584
Egg.

224
00:07:39,667 --> 00:07:40,501
EGG TABLE

225
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:42,170
It's nice. It looks good.

226
00:07:42,253 --> 00:07:43,212
AND…

227
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:44,338
How about this?

228
00:07:46,632 --> 00:07:48,509
Gosh, what a great idea.

229
00:07:48,593 --> 00:07:50,136
After they finish their snacks,

230
00:07:50,219 --> 00:07:51,304
they can play Go.

231
00:07:51,804 --> 00:07:52,847
Nice. Let's put these on.

232
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:53,764
GO BOARD TRAY

233
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:56,642
EVEN A TABLE LAMP THAT SETS THE MOOD

234
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:59,854
<i>Boss gave us such a difficult task to do.</i>

235
00:07:59,937 --> 00:08:01,022
But together,

236
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:05,485
we thought about how to make
the place feel different.

237
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:09,947
I wanted them to enjoy
Kian's incredible imagination

238
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:11,824
as much as possible.

239
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:13,868
The vibe is so different now.

240
00:08:13,951 --> 00:08:15,036
Yeah, it's so nice.

241
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:18,039
Kian, what do you think?
Is this good enough?

242
00:08:18,122 --> 00:08:19,290
You did a great job.

243
00:08:20,374 --> 00:08:21,501
- Okay.
- We did it.

244
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:22,668
MISSION ACCOMPLISHED

245
00:08:22,752 --> 00:08:24,754
Once the food's ready,
we'll be done in no time.

246
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:27,924
Only the pasta's left.
I'm pretty confident about it.

247
00:08:28,007 --> 00:08:29,217
HOT PEPPER SAUCE TUNA PASTA

248
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:30,510
ADDING TUNA TO TOMATO SAUCE

249
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:32,345
- Once the sauce simmers, I'm done.
- Really?

250
00:08:32,428 --> 00:08:35,723
Now, stir it. You have to stir it in.

251
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:38,142
We need to bring this down as is.

252
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:39,852
YEON-KOUNG'S HOT PEPPER SAUCE TUNA PASTA

253
00:08:41,145 --> 00:08:42,104
The place looks nice.

254
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:43,022
- Right?
- Yeah.

255
00:08:43,105 --> 00:08:44,065
I think it's perfect.

256
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:46,776
Now, the glasses.
We just need to rinse them.

257
00:08:46,859 --> 00:08:48,319
LAST THING IS CLEANING WINE GLASSES

258
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:50,905
Gosh, we put in a lot of work.

259
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,699
- Maybe too much.
- Too much.

260
00:08:54,575 --> 00:08:55,701
LUGE TEAM RETURNS AFTER TRIP

261
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:57,328
This will be our last time here now.

262
00:08:57,411 --> 00:08:59,413
We're checking out tomorrow.

263
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:00,790
One, two, three.

264
00:09:00,873 --> 00:09:01,999
- Nice.
- We're used to it now.

265
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:02,917
EASILY

266
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,835
- We're back, Mr. Kian.
- We're back.

267
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:05,878
Welcome back.

268
00:09:07,922 --> 00:09:08,756
What's this?

269
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:11,259
It looks like a campground.

270
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:13,553
This is awesome.

271
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:16,847
They already sound excited.

272
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:18,432
See? The reaction's different.

273
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:22,770
- He's satisfied.
- He likes it.

274
00:09:22,853 --> 00:09:25,690
He laughs like that when he's satisfied.

275
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:26,607
He's happy.

276
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:28,150
Things are going as planned.

277
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:29,986
He loves it.

278
00:09:30,069 --> 00:09:31,362
Let's give it a try.

279
00:09:34,991 --> 00:09:36,701
YOO-MIN, KOTARO,
SUNG-NAM, SEONG-JUN RETURN

280
00:09:36,784 --> 00:09:37,618
Thank you.

281
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,496
- Hello.
- Hello.

282
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:42,331
This is amazing.

283
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:43,416
What's this?

284
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:45,793
EVERYONE'S BACK

285
00:09:45,876 --> 00:09:47,461
This looks incredible.

286
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:49,088
Help yourselves to the food, everyone.

287
00:09:49,171 --> 00:09:50,089
Yes, help yourselves.

288
00:09:50,673 --> 00:09:51,882
Yes, you can serve yourselves.

289
00:09:51,966 --> 00:09:52,800
LIKE AN AWARDS SHOW?

290
00:09:52,883 --> 00:09:54,051
I'll scoop the pasta for you.

291
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:55,177
MAIN CHEF SERVES THE PASTA

292
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:57,138
- Thank you.
- Sure.

293
00:09:57,221 --> 00:09:58,472
- You can have seconds.
- Okay.

294
00:09:58,556 --> 00:10:01,350
- Taro gets a lot for his big appetite.
- Thank you.

295
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:03,102
This has tuna.

296
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:04,729
It's delicious.

297
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:11,193
Is the pasta okay? How is it?

298
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:12,194
It's good.

299
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:13,112
Is the pasta okay?

300
00:10:13,195 --> 00:10:14,530
It's nice and rich.

301
00:10:15,197 --> 00:10:16,282
This is good, Yeon-koung.

302
00:10:16,365 --> 00:10:17,199
Try it.

303
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:19,910
SHE SITS DOWN LAST
AFTER CHECKING THEIR RESPONSES

304
00:10:19,994 --> 00:10:22,455
Everyone, it's your last night,
so let's have a toast.

305
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:23,372
- Sure.
- All right.

306
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:26,250
The night is long, so take your time.

307
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:27,918
You can have some beer,

308
00:10:28,002 --> 00:10:30,087
and I hope you enjoy your last night.

309
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:33,716
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

310
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:35,801
- It's been a pleasure.
- It's been a pleasure.

311
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:37,303
HAPPY KIAN'S B&B DAY IS OPEN

312
00:10:37,386 --> 00:10:38,721
Thank you.

313
00:10:38,804 --> 00:10:40,139
Thank you very much.

314
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:41,223
Thank you.

315
00:10:41,307 --> 00:10:42,350
Cheers.

316
00:10:42,433 --> 00:10:44,101
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

317
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:48,397
Hey, what do you think of this?

318
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:50,149
Compared to eating on the floor?

319
00:10:50,232 --> 00:10:51,817
I love camping vibes.

320
00:10:51,901 --> 00:10:54,153
- Okay. This vibe?
- So I love this atmosphere.

321
00:10:54,236 --> 00:10:55,071
I love it.

322
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:55,988
PROUD

323
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:57,573
Are you going to sing today?

324
00:10:57,657 --> 00:10:58,658
- Sing?
- No pressure.

325
00:10:58,741 --> 00:10:59,575
NERVOUS

326
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:01,452
When do we start? At 8:00 p.m.?

327
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:04,372
Let's start at around 8:00 p.m.

328
00:11:04,455 --> 00:11:05,581
KARAOKE OPENS AT 8:00 P.M.

329
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:06,791
MEANWHILE, AT ANOTHER TABLE

330
00:11:06,874 --> 00:11:08,709
When did you start doing lu…

331
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:10,586
- Luge.
- Yes, luge.

332
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:13,089
Not that long ago. We started last year.

333
00:11:13,172 --> 00:11:14,131
That's right.

334
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:18,094
They started last year,
and they're already on the national team.

335
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:19,428
That's amazing.

336
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:20,721
Want to see my run?

337
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:21,680
Yeah, show us.

338
00:11:21,764 --> 00:11:23,057
This is the start.

339
00:11:23,682 --> 00:11:25,142
It's so fast.

340
00:11:25,226 --> 00:11:26,560
They're going so fast.

341
00:11:26,644 --> 00:11:28,104
It looks pretty dangerous.

342
00:11:28,187 --> 00:11:29,438
We do get injured often.

343
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:33,025
I bumped into a wall here
and got knocked off.

344
00:11:33,109 --> 00:11:33,943
What?

345
00:11:35,152 --> 00:11:36,028
Like this.

346
00:11:38,906 --> 00:11:41,117
Athletes sure are different.

347
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:43,244
How did they even think of doing this?

348
00:11:43,327 --> 00:11:47,957
But to become a member
of the national team

349
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:49,417
is a great honor.

350
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:50,751
- Right.
- It's a huge honor.

351
00:11:51,335 --> 00:11:53,629
- How is the pasta?
- It's good.

352
00:11:53,712 --> 00:11:56,715
I've never eaten this much pasta before.

353
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:57,883
- Really?
- Yes.

354
00:11:57,967 --> 00:11:59,427
You don't have pasta often?

355
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:01,011
Only with my daughters.

356
00:12:01,095 --> 00:12:02,471
Would you like some kimchi?

357
00:12:04,223 --> 00:12:05,558
KIMCHI?

358
00:12:05,641 --> 00:12:07,351
I wasn't thinking about it,

359
00:12:07,435 --> 00:12:10,187
but now that you've mentioned it,
I'm craving kimchi.

360
00:12:10,271 --> 00:12:11,105
I'll bring you some.

361
00:12:11,188 --> 00:12:12,064
GETTING UP

362
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:14,692
PERSONAL SIDE DISH SERVICE
FROM MAIN CHEF

363
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:16,902
It's kimchi. Give it to Mr. Lee.

364
00:12:17,486 --> 00:12:18,821
SEONG-JUN DELIVERS IT

365
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:21,866
Please enjoy.

366
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:23,451
He's been saying all day long,

367
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:25,202
"I want to hang out with Kazuha."

368
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:26,620
GASPING

369
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:28,247
Really? Let's talk.

370
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:29,165
Please sit.

371
00:12:29,248 --> 00:12:30,082
SEONG-JUN JOINS

372
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:31,208
Did you have fun today?

373
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:32,668
We played "Would You Rather" too.

374
00:12:32,751 --> 00:12:34,211
Let's play it now.

375
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:35,838
IT'S "WOULD YOU RATHER" TIME AGAIN

376
00:12:35,921 --> 00:12:37,423
You can ask us questions.

377
00:12:37,506 --> 00:12:38,799
- For you two?
- Yes.

378
00:12:38,883 --> 00:12:40,468
LOOKING FORWARD TO IT

379
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:42,386
Something simple. You know, like…

380
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,638
A penniless

381
00:12:44,722 --> 00:12:46,515
or in debt…

382
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:47,850
Park Bo-gum?

383
00:12:47,933 --> 00:12:48,767
What?

384
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:52,188
So it's a "Would You Rather"
about your ideal romantic type?

385
00:12:52,771 --> 00:12:53,939
SERIOUS

386
00:12:54,023 --> 00:12:55,149
This is so funny.

387
00:12:55,232 --> 00:12:57,193
- You're impossible, Mr. Lee.
- He is.

388
00:12:57,276 --> 00:12:59,028
Right? Isn't he unbelievable?

389
00:12:59,111 --> 00:13:01,071
Or with ten billion won…

390
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,698
You have to pick a good opponent.

391
00:13:03,282 --> 00:13:04,742
I think Park Bo-gum would be better.

392
00:13:04,825 --> 00:13:06,952
I can just pay off
the 10 billion for Bo-gum.

393
00:13:10,831 --> 00:13:11,957
She's on a different level.

394
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:14,084
"I'll just earn the money."

395
00:13:16,295 --> 00:13:17,713
Give us one more.

396
00:13:17,796 --> 00:13:18,672
One more?

397
00:13:18,756 --> 00:13:20,132
Under current circumstances,

398
00:13:20,966 --> 00:13:22,343
you two switch your careers.

399
00:13:22,426 --> 00:13:24,845
- You become Kazuha.
- Right, Kazuha.

400
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:26,597
And you take her career as a K-pop idol.

401
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:28,641
But your entire volleyball career is gone.

402
00:13:28,724 --> 00:13:29,600
Gone?

403
00:13:29,683 --> 00:13:34,063
And you become a volleyball player
who reigns as the world's best.

404
00:13:34,146 --> 00:13:35,314
I become a volleyball player?

405
00:13:35,397 --> 00:13:37,149
But ballet and everything else are gone.

406
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:38,734
- LE SSERAFIM's gone too.
- My gosh.

407
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:40,444
- Will you switch or not switch?
- Okay.

408
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:41,612
- Yes or no.
- Okay.

409
00:13:41,695 --> 00:13:43,822
WORLD-CLASS VOLLEYBALL PLAYER
VS. GLOBAL GIRL GROUP

410
00:13:44,532 --> 00:13:45,449
- Ready?
- Yes.

411
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:46,492
One, two, three.

412
00:13:46,575 --> 00:13:47,576
Yes.

413
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,744
YES, NO

414
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:49,787
- Seriously?
- Yes.

415
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:50,704
GENUINELY SURPRISED

416
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:51,705
Hold on.

417
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:54,667
But why?

418
00:13:54,750 --> 00:13:56,418
I want to be delicate and graceful.

419
00:13:57,002 --> 00:13:58,087
You know…

420
00:13:58,754 --> 00:14:00,422
That would suit you well.

421
00:14:01,757 --> 00:14:03,008
I want to do this for once.

422
00:14:03,092 --> 00:14:04,093
And give up your career?

423
00:14:04,176 --> 00:14:06,136
- It's fine.
- No way.

424
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,638
I've already experienced this life.

425
00:14:07,721 --> 00:14:10,724
- Come on. Really?
- So I know what it feels like.

426
00:14:10,808 --> 00:14:12,226
But I don't know this life.

427
00:14:12,309 --> 00:14:13,644
Why did you say no then?

428
00:14:13,727 --> 00:14:16,230
Me? If I took on her career,

429
00:14:16,313 --> 00:14:19,108
I'd have to keep walking that path.

430
00:14:19,191 --> 00:14:20,609
I wasn't sure I could do that.

431
00:14:21,402 --> 00:14:23,320
- To maintain that career?
- Yes.

432
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:28,325
I am curious though.

433
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:29,243
Right?

434
00:14:31,704 --> 00:14:33,330
We decided earlier to do the dishes.

435
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:34,290
We'll go do them now.

436
00:14:34,373 --> 00:14:36,333
Thank you so much.

437
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:39,378
DINNER COMES TO AN END

438
00:14:39,461 --> 00:14:41,589
YEON-KOUNG AND SUNG-NAM
TAKE CARE OF LEFTOVERS

439
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:44,174
You can just give it to me. Thank you.

440
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:46,802
ZUHA AND SEONG-JUN DO THE DISHES

441
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:49,138
- Shall we talk to them?
- Sure.

442
00:14:49,805 --> 00:14:50,681
Is everything okay?

443
00:14:50,764 --> 00:14:51,599
Yes.

444
00:14:51,682 --> 00:14:54,727
Today, in the morning…

445
00:14:54,810 --> 00:14:56,312
- Yes?
- Why…

446
00:14:56,395 --> 00:14:57,354
The gym…

447
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:02,276
No work out?

448
00:15:02,359 --> 00:15:03,277
It's tiring.

449
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,445
"It's tiring."

450
00:15:04,528 --> 00:15:06,238
It's tiring.

451
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:07,531
Your Korean's so good.

452
00:15:07,615 --> 00:15:09,116
It's gotten better from yesterday.

453
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:10,326
Right?

454
00:15:10,409 --> 00:15:11,744
It's improving day by day.

455
00:15:11,827 --> 00:15:13,537
It must be a survival instinct

456
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:15,497
because he has to
keep speaking Korean here.

457
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:18,292
Are you active in Japan these days?

458
00:15:18,375 --> 00:15:20,586
Is that why you can still speak Japanese?

459
00:15:20,669 --> 00:15:21,837
Not lately.

460
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:26,258
But last year in Japan, at an arena…

461
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:27,635
An arena tour?

462
00:15:27,718 --> 00:15:31,138
It wasn't a tour.
I only did two performances.

463
00:15:31,221 --> 00:15:34,558
BUT LAST YEAR IN JAPAN, AT AN ARENA…

464
00:15:34,642 --> 00:15:36,727
"For three years, in Japan…"

465
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:38,479
- Arena? Arena tour?
- Yes.

466
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:40,356
"I was there"?

467
00:15:40,439 --> 00:15:41,774
I only did two…

468
00:15:41,857 --> 00:15:43,150
"I didn't forget."

469
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:45,235
A concert for fans.

470
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:47,071
"Concerts."

471
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:49,114
"Just a bit, so…"

472
00:15:49,198 --> 00:15:51,909
HAVING A LISTENING TEST BY HIMSELF

473
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:53,869
Translate it.

474
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:55,829
- I'm studying right now.
- He's translating it.

475
00:15:55,913 --> 00:15:58,666
They're too fast for me,
but I can hear you a little.

476
00:15:58,749 --> 00:16:02,252
I try to be active in Japan every year
whenever I have the chance.

477
00:16:02,878 --> 00:16:04,171
<i>"Yattemasu."</i>

478
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:05,381
"I was there"?

479
00:16:06,882 --> 00:16:08,550
Let me go study for a bit. This won't do.

480
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:12,346
- All right, that was a great meal.
- Let's go.

481
00:16:12,429 --> 00:16:14,139
KIAN'S B&B

482
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:16,016
Boss, didn't you say we'd open it?

483
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:17,059
Right, let's do it.

484
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:27,486
JUN-HO PREPARES TO OPEN THE KARAOKE ROOM

485
00:16:27,569 --> 00:16:28,654
I'll turn the lights off.

486
00:16:29,238 --> 00:16:30,072
There we go.

487
00:16:31,031 --> 00:16:34,910
THE BOSS CHANGES INTO HIS SUIT

488
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:39,915
WASHES HIS FACE

489
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,501
AND TIDIES HIS HAIR

490
00:16:42,584 --> 00:16:46,171
ONCE AGAIN

491
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:57,474
ALL EYES ON HIM

492
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:58,392
What?

493
00:17:00,352 --> 00:17:01,687
You look clean-cut.

494
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:04,690
Isn't that the suit he wore
when he sang "Stay With Me"?

495
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:05,941
You look so cool.

496
00:17:06,984 --> 00:17:08,569
You're a little too dolled up.

497
00:17:08,652 --> 00:17:10,279
I only put water in my hair.

498
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:12,364
What are you talking about?

499
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:14,283
Everyone.

500
00:17:15,075 --> 00:17:18,287
The opening
of Kian's B&B Karaoke begins now.

501
00:17:18,370 --> 00:17:19,830
Please give a big round of applause.

502
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:25,377
KIAN'S B&B KARAOKE

503
00:17:25,461 --> 00:17:27,087
First of all,

504
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:30,132
we want to give a huge thank you
to everyone who came here.

505
00:17:30,215 --> 00:17:31,425
HOST LEE JUN-HO

506
00:17:31,508 --> 00:17:34,595
There's someone
who put a lot of work into this night.

507
00:17:34,678 --> 00:17:37,556
I'd like to introduce our boss, Mr. Kian.

508
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:39,183
Let's give him a big hand.

509
00:17:44,229 --> 00:17:46,857
The final night has come at last.

510
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:48,150
Are you sad?

511
00:17:48,233 --> 00:17:49,902
- Yes!
- Yes!

512
00:17:49,985 --> 00:17:51,653
Well, that can't be helped though.

513
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:55,324
You all have to check out
and go back home tomorrow.

514
00:17:55,407 --> 00:17:56,533
No!

515
00:17:57,951 --> 00:18:00,204
To Kian's B&B,

516
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:01,163
she's our fairy.

517
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:04,249
Let me introduce Kazuha to the stage.

518
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:08,712
- They're going to sing a duet tonight.
- Really?

519
00:18:08,796 --> 00:18:10,839
THE BOSS AND ZUHA'S DUET PERFORMANCE?

520
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:11,924
DURING AFTERNOON MEETING

521
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:14,885
I think we should go first
when we open the karaoke room.

522
00:18:14,968 --> 00:18:19,181
You and Zuha wanted to do
a duet anyway, right?

523
00:18:19,264 --> 00:18:20,766
- Are you okay with it?
- Yeah, I'm in.

524
00:18:20,849 --> 00:18:22,601
THE BOSS AND ZUHA TEAM UP

525
00:18:23,435 --> 00:18:25,729
What's your favorite song?

526
00:18:25,813 --> 00:18:28,148
I was going to sing "Akai Sweet Pea."

527
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:29,358
"Akai…"

528
00:18:29,441 --> 00:18:31,401
- "Sweet Pea."
- "Sweet…"

529
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:33,070
I've never heard of this song.

530
00:18:33,153 --> 00:18:36,949
HE PRACTICED THE WHOLE TIME IN THE CAR

531
00:18:38,075 --> 00:18:39,952
Everyone, how has your stay been?

532
00:18:40,035 --> 00:18:42,079
- It's been great!
- It's been great!

533
00:18:42,162 --> 00:18:43,247
Were you happy?

534
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:45,124
- Yes!
- Yes!

535
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:46,750
You sure you won't forget this?

536
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:48,293
- We won't!
- We won't!

537
00:18:50,379 --> 00:18:51,672
"AKAI SWEET PEA"
BY SEIKO MATSUDA

538
00:18:51,755 --> 00:18:53,549
- We won't skip the intro.
- Okay.

539
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:58,303
HE MAKES AWKWARD GESTURES AGAIN

540
00:19:01,014 --> 00:19:02,933
Why are you looking at me?
Look over there.

541
00:19:03,016 --> 00:19:04,434
I thought you were doing something.

542
00:19:05,102 --> 00:19:06,145
This is nice!

543
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:08,355
So nice!

544
00:19:11,066 --> 00:19:12,317
Let's give them a hand here.

545
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:17,865
Let's do the wave.

546
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:18,782
The wave!

547
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:28,458
<i>I'll gently snuggle up to your shirt</i>

548
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:32,337
<i>That smells of cigarettes</i>

549
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:35,340
<i>It's been…</i>

550
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:37,176
STAMMERING

551
00:19:37,259 --> 00:19:38,218
What was it?

552
00:19:40,095 --> 00:19:41,805
ZUHA, HELP ME

553
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:42,973
<i>Since we met</i>

554
00:19:43,056 --> 00:19:47,060
<i>Why haven't you even held my hand?</i>

555
00:19:47,144 --> 00:19:48,145
ZUHA JOINS IN

556
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:53,942
<i>With boots that have wings</i>

557
00:19:55,861 --> 00:20:01,658
<i>I want to run through our youth with you</i>

558
00:20:01,742 --> 00:20:05,287
- Kazuha!
- Kazuha!

559
00:20:05,954 --> 00:20:11,376
<i>The flower buds by the railway are</i>

560
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:15,005
<i>Red sweet peas</i>

561
00:20:15,088 --> 00:20:19,343
<i>I love you more</i>

562
00:20:19,426 --> 00:20:20,594
My goodness.

563
00:20:20,677 --> 00:20:22,137
<i>Than anyone I've met so far</i>

564
00:20:23,847 --> 00:20:27,476
<i>I love your way of life</i>

565
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:33,190
<i>I can't go back like this</i>

566
00:20:33,273 --> 00:20:36,193
<i>I can't go back</i>

567
00:20:36,944 --> 00:20:42,449
<i>On the day spring came to my heart</i>

568
00:20:42,532 --> 00:20:48,121
<i>There were red sweet peas</i>

569
00:20:51,124 --> 00:20:52,709
Good job!

570
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:55,003
Encore!

571
00:20:55,712 --> 00:20:57,464
That was great.

572
00:20:58,966 --> 00:21:00,676
What a beautiful night.

573
00:21:02,344 --> 00:21:03,220
How nice.

574
00:21:05,973 --> 00:21:06,807
BUMMED

575
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:07,724
I messed up a lot.

576
00:21:07,808 --> 00:21:08,809
You were fine.

577
00:21:08,892 --> 00:21:10,352
You sang it really well.

578
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:11,478
Great job.

579
00:21:11,561 --> 00:21:13,855
- Was it okay?
- Yeah, you did well.

580
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:15,399
Yes, good job.

581
00:21:16,066 --> 00:21:18,068
- I didn't know the lyrics.
- That was great!

582
00:21:18,151 --> 00:21:20,195
- Seriously.
- That was great.

583
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:22,114
- That was so good.
- It was?

584
00:21:22,197 --> 00:21:23,365
Boss, good job.

585
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:24,491
- Yeah?
- That's right.

586
00:21:24,574 --> 00:21:26,201
Taro was grateful for the Japanese.

587
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:27,202
- I'm so happy.
- Really?

588
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:29,162
- I'm really happy. Thank you.
- So happy.

589
00:21:31,164 --> 00:21:32,708
Shall we drink together?

590
00:21:32,791 --> 00:21:35,168
Let's drink. Cheers.

591
00:21:35,752 --> 00:21:37,087
WITH THEIR DUET PERFORMANCE

592
00:21:37,170 --> 00:21:38,005
Cheers.

593
00:21:38,088 --> 00:21:41,800
HAPPY KIAN'S B&B DAY BEGINS IN EARNEST

594
00:21:41,883 --> 00:21:43,677
THEY SING IN THE KARAOKE ROOM

595
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:44,803
Cheers.

596
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:47,639
THE OTHERS BELOW HAVE FUN
IN THEIR OWN WAYS

597
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:52,811
It suddenly feels like a live music bar.

598
00:21:52,894 --> 00:21:54,396
Isn't that what you wanted?

599
00:21:54,479 --> 00:21:55,856
THE CASUAL VIBE THE BOSS WANTED

600
00:21:55,939 --> 00:21:57,649
EXCITED

601
00:21:58,817 --> 00:22:00,527
KARAOKE GOES ON WITHOUT ANY BREAKS

602
00:22:00,610 --> 00:22:02,112
Bravo!

603
00:22:02,946 --> 00:22:05,490
EVEN A SPECIAL BODYBUILDING PERFORMANCE

604
00:22:07,826 --> 00:22:08,952
Way to go!

605
00:22:11,455 --> 00:22:12,873
There you go!

606
00:22:14,249 --> 00:22:16,626
HAPPY KIAN'S B&B DAY
GETS EVEN MORE EXCITING

607
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:21,256
HAPPY KIAN GETS EVEN MORE EXCITED

608
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:22,924
This is so nice.

609
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:23,842
Yeah.

610
00:22:23,925 --> 00:22:26,970
You know, it's so nice
to see you feeling happy.

611
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:28,805
- Really?
- Yeah.

612
00:22:28,889 --> 00:22:30,766
I hope he stays like this.

613
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:34,186
I can see how worried
you've been about this.

614
00:22:34,269 --> 00:22:36,521
Yeah, I've been so…

615
00:22:38,398 --> 00:22:39,608
- What is it?
- The karaoke…

616
00:22:39,691 --> 00:22:41,318
Would it feel too forced?

617
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:42,903
KARAOKE WORRIED HIM

618
00:22:42,986 --> 00:22:44,946
- I've lost a lot of confidence.
- Really?

619
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:45,864
Yeah.

620
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:48,909
I'm happy. But it's not just me, right?

621
00:22:48,992 --> 00:22:50,035
- Cheers.
- Yeah.

622
00:22:50,118 --> 00:22:51,620
Cheers.

623
00:22:53,038 --> 00:22:55,582
Cheers.

624
00:22:55,665 --> 00:22:57,209
- Incredible.
- Cheers.

625
00:22:57,292 --> 00:23:04,007
MAXIMUM HAPPINESS

626
00:23:04,091 --> 00:23:06,468
Let's sleep in tomorrow.

627
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:09,137
FLICK

628
00:23:09,221 --> 00:23:10,764
Hey, this will be so sweet for you.

629
00:23:10,847 --> 00:23:13,266
You have free time
until 11:00 a.m. tomorrow.

630
00:23:13,350 --> 00:23:14,184
That's a sweet deal.

631
00:23:14,267 --> 00:23:15,310
THEY DOUBT IT

632
00:23:15,393 --> 00:23:19,022
If you want, you can go home
and come back by 11:00 a.m. tomorrow.

633
00:23:19,106 --> 00:23:20,774
You can even fit in your own plans.

634
00:23:20,857 --> 00:23:23,026
Do as you please.
You'll have plenty of time.

635
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:25,237
- Is free time until 11:00 a.m. okay?
- Sure.

636
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:26,154
FLICK

637
00:23:26,738 --> 00:23:28,115
I thought you didn't see it.

638
00:23:29,991 --> 00:23:31,451
Yeon-koung.

639
00:23:31,535 --> 00:23:32,953
What is it?

640
00:23:33,036 --> 00:23:35,664
I'm grateful
that you're following my lead.

641
00:23:36,748 --> 00:23:37,582
All of a sudden?

642
00:23:38,166 --> 00:23:40,085
I thought you'd want to be the leader.

643
00:23:40,168 --> 00:23:41,128
What do you mean?

644
00:23:41,211 --> 00:23:43,171
Since you've always been a leader

645
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:45,257
as a captain of a team or a coach.

646
00:23:46,341 --> 00:23:50,428
I thought you'd look at me and think,
"This punk is a terrible leader."

647
00:23:51,304 --> 00:23:53,431
But that person supports you.

648
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:54,516
She's so respectful.

649
00:23:54,599 --> 00:23:55,433
Yes, sir.

650
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:56,476
"Yes, Boss."

651
00:23:57,269 --> 00:23:59,563
Yeah, and she's like that
because you're the boss.

652
00:23:59,646 --> 00:24:02,107
- But it always makes me nervous.
- Why?

653
00:24:02,732 --> 00:24:05,152
Because I get worried
about letting you down.

654
00:24:05,235 --> 00:24:06,403
Really?

655
00:24:06,486 --> 00:24:07,779
SHE DIDN'T KNOW HOW HE FELT

656
00:24:07,863 --> 00:24:11,116
It makes me work harder
to not be just an owner in name only.

657
00:24:11,199 --> 00:24:12,742
Come on, she'd never think that.

658
00:24:12,826 --> 00:24:14,119
- You're doing your best.
- Yeah.

659
00:24:14,202 --> 00:24:15,704
- You're doing a good job.
- Right.

660
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:17,873
So if it gets hard for you,
I'll guide you.

661
00:24:17,956 --> 00:24:19,166
Just follow my lead.

662
00:24:23,336 --> 00:24:24,379
GLANCING

663
00:24:24,963 --> 00:24:26,214
How have you been holding up?

664
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:27,716
I've become more comfortable now.

665
00:24:27,799 --> 00:24:29,759
- You're okay?
- Because you try to put me at ease.

666
00:24:29,843 --> 00:24:30,677
- Yeah?
- Yes.

667
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:32,304
- She does well on her own now.
- Yeah.

668
00:24:32,387 --> 00:24:34,598
I like that you feel
comfortable around us.

669
00:24:35,182 --> 00:24:37,976
- I like how friendly you are.
- Right.

670
00:24:38,059 --> 00:24:40,020
THE BOSS IS GRATEFUL
THAT ZUHA ADJUSTED WELL

671
00:24:40,103 --> 00:24:42,564
And I feel sorry to Jun-ho the most.

672
00:24:42,647 --> 00:24:43,899
Why?

673
00:24:43,982 --> 00:24:46,318
He has at least four Band-Aids
on his hands.

674
00:24:46,401 --> 00:24:48,195
I saw him put some ointment on.

675
00:24:50,155 --> 00:24:52,032
JUN-HO WAS ALWAYS WASHING DISHES

676
00:24:52,115 --> 00:24:53,366
Let me use this too.

677
00:24:53,450 --> 00:24:54,284
FIRST-AID KIT

678
00:24:55,410 --> 00:24:56,494
You have blisters.

679
00:24:57,245 --> 00:24:58,663
Is this all from dishwashing?

680
00:24:58,747 --> 00:25:00,790
That and from taking care of the knives.

681
00:25:00,874 --> 00:25:02,709
I got each cut while working.

682
00:25:03,418 --> 00:25:05,921
No, it's not just me.
We've all gotten hurt.

683
00:25:06,004 --> 00:25:08,590
Anyway, I'm the one leading you, but…

684
00:25:08,673 --> 00:25:09,925
SAD

685
00:25:10,008 --> 00:25:11,009
Are you going to cry?

686
00:25:11,092 --> 00:25:12,636
- Are you?
- I will on the last day.

687
00:25:12,719 --> 00:25:13,553
His shoulders…

688
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:15,138
HUNCHED SHOULDERS

689
00:25:15,222 --> 00:25:17,766
Why are your shoulders hunched?
What's wrong?

690
00:25:17,849 --> 00:25:21,019
This is why bosses always want
to have company dinners so much.

691
00:25:21,102 --> 00:25:22,979
It's their chance to talk honestly.

692
00:25:23,063 --> 00:25:24,773
What are you talking about?

693
00:25:24,856 --> 00:25:27,150
This is when they can say
what they've been holding in.

694
00:25:28,818 --> 00:25:29,653
I see.

695
00:25:29,736 --> 00:25:30,737
Last drink.

696
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:31,947
Cheers.

697
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:32,864
12:50 A.M.

698
00:25:32,948 --> 00:25:34,699
Everyone, it'll be lights-out at 1:00 a.m.

699
00:25:34,783 --> 00:25:35,951
- Let's wrap it up.
- Okay.

700
00:25:36,034 --> 00:25:37,619
Kian, is it okay to leave it like this?

701
00:25:37,702 --> 00:25:39,746
Let's clean this up tomorrow morning.

702
00:25:39,829 --> 00:25:41,665
Is anyone sleeping in the middle here?

703
00:25:41,748 --> 00:25:42,749
No.

704
00:25:42,832 --> 00:25:44,000
- Okay.
- No one.

705
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:45,961
THE KARAOKE ROOM CLOSES

706
00:25:46,586 --> 00:25:49,839
THE BOSS TAKES OFF HIS SUIT

707
00:25:50,507 --> 00:25:52,884
TV CABINET

708
00:25:53,426 --> 00:25:56,096
NEXT TO THE RAMYEON BOXES

709
00:25:56,179 --> 00:25:59,349
WINDOWSILL
FRIDGE

710
00:26:00,350 --> 00:26:01,309
Good night.

711
00:26:01,393 --> 00:26:02,227
Sleep tight.

712
00:26:02,310 --> 00:26:04,145
THE STAFF GOES TO BED TOO

713
00:26:04,229 --> 00:26:05,480
Good work, Kian.

714
00:26:05,563 --> 00:26:06,773
Hey, get some sleep.

715
00:26:06,856 --> 00:26:07,691
Okay.

716
00:26:14,739 --> 00:26:17,033
IT'S DRIZZLING

717
00:26:17,117 --> 00:26:19,911
DAY 6

718
00:26:19,995 --> 00:26:22,580
9:00 A.M.

719
00:26:24,624 --> 00:26:26,459
REMNANTS OF A BIZARRE MESS

720
00:26:26,543 --> 00:26:28,169
ALL OVER THE PLACE

721
00:26:29,796 --> 00:26:32,257
JUN-HO WAKES UP

722
00:26:37,053 --> 00:26:39,014
STILL RETURNING TO REALITY

723
00:26:40,473 --> 00:26:42,684
JUN-HO GOES TO WASH UP FIRST

724
00:26:42,767 --> 00:26:44,269
YEON-KOUNG IS UP

725
00:26:47,314 --> 00:26:48,315
Did you sleep well?

726
00:26:48,398 --> 00:26:49,607
Yes, good morning.

727
00:26:51,484 --> 00:26:53,278
WHILE EMPLOYEES WASH UP

728
00:26:54,195 --> 00:26:55,488
Let's turn the lights on now.

729
00:26:58,575 --> 00:27:01,202
SUDDEN FLASH

730
00:27:05,832 --> 00:27:07,834
THE BOSS GETS UP

731
00:27:12,172 --> 00:27:14,257
HE GOES TO WASH UP TOO

732
00:27:15,717 --> 00:27:17,344
HE FINISHES SHOWERING

733
00:27:21,181 --> 00:27:22,932
This will take forever to clean up.

734
00:27:24,267 --> 00:27:25,894
11:00 A.M. CHECK-OUT TIME APPROACHES

735
00:27:25,977 --> 00:27:27,729
We should clean it up then.

736
00:27:31,232 --> 00:27:33,193
HIS GRAY SWEATSHIRT
THAT THE EMPLOYEES WASHED

737
00:27:34,027 --> 00:27:35,278
CLEANUP BEGINS

738
00:27:35,987 --> 00:27:37,572
CLEANUP LIST
CLEAR THE TRASH

739
00:27:38,239 --> 00:27:40,325
Let's throw these away too.

740
00:27:40,909 --> 00:27:41,993
Kian, open it up for me.

741
00:27:42,077 --> 00:27:43,161
THE GUESTS HELP TOO

742
00:27:43,244 --> 00:27:45,872
COLLECT FOOD WASTE

743
00:27:46,581 --> 00:27:48,541
It's so fast when we do it together.

744
00:27:48,625 --> 00:27:50,293
FOLD UP THE FURNITURE

745
00:27:50,377 --> 00:27:52,670
RETURN TABLES AND CHAIRS
TO ORIGINAL PLACES

746
00:27:52,754 --> 00:27:53,713
All done.

747
00:27:53,797 --> 00:27:54,756
Let's go.

748
00:27:54,839 --> 00:27:57,300
It's the staff's job,
but thank you so much for the help.

749
00:27:57,384 --> 00:27:59,928
KIAN'S B&B HAS BECOME NEAT AND CLEAN

750
00:28:01,846 --> 00:28:04,391
HE CLEANS HIS TEETH TOO

751
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:09,813
THINKING

752
00:28:09,896 --> 00:28:11,106
HE PUTS IT IN THE BAG

753
00:28:14,526 --> 00:28:16,820
AND A CLEAN SHAVE

754
00:28:28,957 --> 00:28:30,250
GUESTS GET READY TO CHECK OUT

755
00:28:30,333 --> 00:28:32,293
I'll pack my stuff first.

756
00:28:32,377 --> 00:28:34,254
I was so glad a Japanese person was here.

757
00:28:34,337 --> 00:28:36,297
- Really?
- I was relieved.

758
00:28:36,381 --> 00:28:38,341
I worried no Japanese people
would be here.

759
00:28:38,425 --> 00:28:39,384
Really?

760
00:28:39,467 --> 00:28:41,594
I thought it'd be hard to communicate.

761
00:28:41,678 --> 00:28:42,846
Thank you so much.

762
00:28:42,929 --> 00:28:44,180
It was my pleasure.

763
00:28:45,348 --> 00:28:46,891
It's time to check out now.

764
00:28:46,975 --> 00:28:48,476
Say a few words, Boss.

765
00:28:50,520 --> 00:28:52,814
When I first made this,

766
00:28:52,897 --> 00:28:54,816
I thought guests would just be guests.

767
00:28:54,899 --> 00:28:58,486
But now, it feels like
we become a sort of family.

768
00:28:58,570 --> 00:29:01,656
So when you leave,
it makes me feel a bit sad.

769
00:29:02,657 --> 00:29:03,908
I wish you happiness.

770
00:29:03,992 --> 00:29:05,243
- Time to check out.
- Okay.

771
00:29:05,326 --> 00:29:06,286
EVERYONE CHECKS OUT

772
00:29:06,369 --> 00:29:07,829
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

773
00:29:07,912 --> 00:29:08,747
Thank you so much.

774
00:29:08,830 --> 00:29:10,290
See you again.

775
00:29:12,500 --> 00:29:13,626
We'll get going.

776
00:29:14,210 --> 00:29:15,336
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

777
00:29:16,004 --> 00:29:18,006
SIGHING

778
00:29:18,089 --> 00:29:19,883
Hey, Jin-an. Don't cry.

779
00:29:19,966 --> 00:29:20,800
I'm not crying.

780
00:29:20,884 --> 00:29:21,968
Don't cry, okay?

781
00:29:22,051 --> 00:29:23,094
I'm not crying.

782
00:29:23,178 --> 00:29:24,721
Come on, don't do that!

783
00:29:24,804 --> 00:29:27,223
All right. I'll open the door for you.

784
00:29:29,225 --> 00:29:30,602
Bye, Taro.

785
00:29:30,685 --> 00:29:32,103
- Bye, Yoo-min.
- Thank you.

786
00:29:32,187 --> 00:29:33,563
- Thank you.
- Bye.

787
00:29:33,646 --> 00:29:35,064
- Take care.
- Bye.

788
00:29:35,148 --> 00:29:36,524
I'll be back with a medal.

789
00:29:36,608 --> 00:29:37,442
- Bye.
- Goodbye.

790
00:29:37,525 --> 00:29:39,027
Bye, Gi-pyo.

791
00:29:39,110 --> 00:29:40,945
- Bye, Kian.
- Thank you.

792
00:29:41,029 --> 00:29:41,863
- Bye.
- Bye.

793
00:29:41,946 --> 00:29:43,448
- Goodbye.
- Bye. Thank you.

794
00:29:43,531 --> 00:29:44,616
ALL SEVEN GUESTS CHECK OUT

795
00:29:44,699 --> 00:29:46,326
We're all leaving. This feels weird.

796
00:29:47,076 --> 00:29:48,286
Man, all of us are leaving.

797
00:29:48,369 --> 00:29:50,663
It feels as if we'll come back
later today.

798
00:29:51,247 --> 00:29:52,665
It was fun.

799
00:29:52,749 --> 00:29:54,667
<i>As I expected, it was so fun.</i>

800
00:29:54,751 --> 00:29:57,921
Since my Korean isn't very good,

801
00:29:58,004 --> 00:30:00,840
I thought it'd be hard to communicate.

802
00:30:00,924 --> 00:30:02,884
Hello.

803
00:30:03,510 --> 00:30:04,886
<i>But they spoke to me in Japanese</i>

804
00:30:04,969 --> 00:30:06,888
<i>and even in body language.</i>

805
00:30:06,971 --> 00:30:08,640
So I was really at ease during my stay.

806
00:30:08,723 --> 00:30:11,643
<i>To me, Kian's B&B is</i>

807
00:30:11,726 --> 00:30:13,353
<i>"the perfect home."</i>

808
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:16,648
<i>Luge is a sport</i>

809
00:30:16,731 --> 00:30:18,691
<i>that's unfamiliar to many people.</i>

810
00:30:18,775 --> 00:30:21,402
<i>And they really wanted</i>
<i>to learn about the sport.</i>

811
00:30:21,486 --> 00:30:25,865
So as we told them about it,
I think it really boosted our confidence.

812
00:30:25,949 --> 00:30:28,034
<i>They cared for us and helped us so much.</i>

813
00:30:28,117 --> 00:30:30,620
<i>I want to give them 200 stars.</i>

814
00:30:30,703 --> 00:30:32,789
When I was young,

815
00:30:32,872 --> 00:30:36,167
I didn't really get to enjoy my childhood.

816
00:30:36,251 --> 00:30:38,044
In children's homes,

817
00:30:38,127 --> 00:30:40,421
around ten kids live together.

818
00:30:40,505 --> 00:30:42,549
There's no personal space.

819
00:30:42,632 --> 00:30:47,428
<i>So I wished I could sleep alone</i>
<i>in a big room when I was young.</i>

820
00:30:47,512 --> 00:30:51,850
<i>And it felt like</i>
<i>my childhood dream had come true.</i>

821
00:30:51,933 --> 00:30:53,935
<i>For three days,</i>
<i>it was as if I got to enjoy</i>

822
00:30:54,018 --> 00:30:56,855
<i>the life I had longed for as a child.</i>

823
00:30:56,938 --> 00:30:59,983
So I think Kian's B&B
is "a child's heart."

824
00:31:00,066 --> 00:31:01,317
We'll get going.

825
00:31:01,401 --> 00:31:02,777
Bye.

826
00:31:03,444 --> 00:31:05,280
That was so fun.

827
00:31:06,948 --> 00:31:08,950
11:10 A.M.

828
00:31:09,784 --> 00:31:10,743
It's quiet.

829
00:31:11,494 --> 00:31:12,328
So quiet.

830
00:31:17,584 --> 00:31:18,418
Today,

831
00:31:19,085 --> 00:31:20,587
we'll clean and organize.

832
00:31:20,670 --> 00:31:22,630
We have time until 4:00 p.m. anyway.

833
00:31:22,714 --> 00:31:24,799
So let's have free time to ourselves.

834
00:31:25,675 --> 00:31:28,219
I think we really need it today.

835
00:31:28,303 --> 00:31:30,138
We need a little time to ourselves.

836
00:31:30,847 --> 00:31:33,141
Yeah, let's have free time.

837
00:31:34,809 --> 00:31:36,144
I guess you've all hit the wall.

838
00:31:36,227 --> 00:31:37,687
Now that it's the fifth day…

839
00:31:37,770 --> 00:31:39,147
IT'S DAY 6
SHE GOT THE DAY WRONG

840
00:31:39,230 --> 00:31:40,481
You're all exhausted.

841
00:31:41,983 --> 00:31:42,817
I'm tired.

842
00:31:47,697 --> 00:31:49,991
Is there anything you want to do
in your spare time?

843
00:31:50,074 --> 00:31:51,284
What about food today?

844
00:31:51,367 --> 00:31:52,785
- Food?
- What do we do?

845
00:31:52,869 --> 00:31:54,579
- For lunch?
- For lunch.

846
00:31:54,662 --> 00:31:56,122
Or we can order in.

847
00:31:56,205 --> 00:31:57,707
We've never ordered lunch before.

848
00:31:57,790 --> 00:31:58,666
- Right.
- Right?

849
00:31:58,750 --> 00:31:59,667
IS IT OKAY?

850
00:31:59,751 --> 00:32:01,461
Let's order in for lunch.

851
00:32:01,544 --> 00:32:02,378
APPROVED

852
00:32:02,462 --> 00:32:03,421
You pick what you want.

853
00:32:03,504 --> 00:32:04,631
BRINGS FOOD DELIVERY BOOKLET

854
00:32:04,714 --> 00:32:06,382
Pork cutlets, lunch boxes…

855
00:32:07,425 --> 00:32:08,551
These look good.

856
00:32:08,635 --> 00:32:10,762
Right. <i>Osam</i> bulgogi sounds good.

857
00:32:10,845 --> 00:32:12,013
It does.

858
00:32:12,889 --> 00:32:13,723
FOCUSED

859
00:32:13,806 --> 00:32:15,475
- What do we eat? <i>Bunsik?</i>
- You want <i>bunsik?</i>

860
00:32:17,810 --> 00:32:20,104
Hey, you know what? First…

861
00:32:23,316 --> 00:32:25,026
Let's use up
all the leftover ingredients.

862
00:32:25,568 --> 00:32:27,236
We have a lot of ingredients.

863
00:32:27,320 --> 00:32:29,489
- Make something with them?
- With what we have?

864
00:32:30,073 --> 00:32:31,741
Is there anything we can make?

865
00:32:31,824 --> 00:32:32,867
<i>Ramyeon.</i> What else?

866
00:32:33,910 --> 00:32:35,912
I'll make it really delicious.

867
00:32:35,995 --> 00:32:37,413
FRUGAL OWNER

868
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:38,748
This looks good too.

869
00:32:38,831 --> 00:32:39,832
CAN'T LET IT GO

870
00:32:39,916 --> 00:32:42,543
- We can't order from here.
- This restaurant doesn't deliver.

871
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:43,920
You don't want <i>ramyeon?</i>

872
00:32:44,587 --> 00:32:46,130
- We do.
- We'll eat it.

873
00:32:51,302 --> 00:32:53,846
There are so many ingredients left.
We have to eat them.

874
00:32:55,848 --> 00:32:57,392
BEGINS TO EMPTY THE FRIDGE

875
00:32:57,475 --> 00:32:59,811
LEFTOVER INGREDIENT 1
CHEONGYANG CHILI PEPPERS

876
00:32:59,894 --> 00:33:03,064
LEFTOVER INGREDIENT 2
BUTTON MUSHROOMS

877
00:33:08,611 --> 00:33:11,155
LEFTOVER INGREDIENT 3
HOT PEPPER SAUCE TUNA

878
00:33:11,781 --> 00:33:14,492
SCATTERING CRUMBS

879
00:33:14,575 --> 00:33:16,536
FRUGAL

880
00:33:17,328 --> 00:33:18,496
LEFTOVER INGREDIENT 4
RAMYEON

881
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:22,041
LAST INGREDIENT
4 EGGS

882
00:33:22,125 --> 00:33:22,959
This looks good.

883
00:33:31,009 --> 00:33:32,969
THE BOSS'S RAMYEON IS READY

884
00:33:38,933 --> 00:33:40,059
Come and eat.

885
00:33:40,601 --> 00:33:41,644
- Okay.
- Okay.

886
00:33:46,441 --> 00:33:47,775
This looks good.

887
00:33:49,318 --> 00:33:50,862
- It looks good.
- Gosh, Boss.

888
00:33:51,654 --> 00:33:52,655
He made it for us.

889
00:33:53,239 --> 00:33:54,907
We had a lot of ingredients.

890
00:33:54,991 --> 00:33:55,825
Thank you.

891
00:33:55,908 --> 00:33:57,160
- Enjoy.
- Bon appétit.

892
00:33:57,243 --> 00:33:58,077
All right.

893
00:33:58,745 --> 00:34:00,121
It looks so good.

894
00:34:00,204 --> 00:34:01,372
- Seriously.
- It looks good.

895
00:34:11,924 --> 00:34:13,551
What kind of <i>ramyeon</i> is this?

896
00:34:13,634 --> 00:34:14,927
- Shin Ramyun.
- It's good.

897
00:34:15,011 --> 00:34:15,845
Yeah.

898
00:34:19,015 --> 00:34:22,560
INHALING

899
00:34:22,643 --> 00:34:23,811
This is so good.

900
00:34:24,604 --> 00:34:26,814
<i>Ramyeon</i> is the best.

901
00:34:27,565 --> 00:34:28,691
You're really enjoying it.

902
00:34:28,775 --> 00:34:29,609
Yeah, it's good.

903
00:34:29,692 --> 00:34:30,526
SNIFFLING

904
00:34:30,610 --> 00:34:31,819
It's a perfect hangover cure.

905
00:34:31,903 --> 00:34:32,779
It's good.

906
00:34:34,155 --> 00:34:36,908
In the end, we ate
what Boss wanted to eat,

907
00:34:37,492 --> 00:34:38,576
not what Zuha wanted.

908
00:34:38,659 --> 00:34:40,036
- Is that how it ended up?
- Yeah.

909
00:34:40,119 --> 00:34:42,705
Zuha looked really hard
through the book to find what to eat.

910
00:34:42,789 --> 00:34:44,373
TEASING

911
00:34:44,457 --> 00:34:45,750
I looked really hard.

912
00:34:46,542 --> 00:34:48,211
You say that after eating all your food?

913
00:34:48,294 --> 00:34:49,128
FLUSTERED

914
00:34:49,212 --> 00:34:50,171
It was good.

915
00:34:50,254 --> 00:34:54,092
You should've told me clearly.
Like, "We're ordering in no matter what."

916
00:34:54,175 --> 00:34:56,469
HUNCHED SHOULDERS AGAIN

917
00:35:00,807 --> 00:35:02,850
- He's looking different from last night.
- Yeah.

918
00:35:02,934 --> 00:35:05,853
He was confident and saying,
"Hey, you should've told me."

919
00:35:05,937 --> 00:35:09,398
"Hey, I now know why bosses want
to have company dinners."

920
00:35:09,482 --> 00:35:10,691
That's right!

921
00:35:10,775 --> 00:35:13,319
"We have to talk honestly over drinks.
Right, Yeon-koung?"

922
00:35:13,402 --> 00:35:15,321
- And he did speak honestly.
- Right.

923
00:35:15,905 --> 00:35:17,532
I tend to change after 10:00 p.m.

924
00:35:18,699 --> 00:35:19,784
We've figured you out now.

925
00:35:19,867 --> 00:35:21,244
Really?

926
00:35:21,327 --> 00:35:22,829
At around that time,

927
00:35:23,496 --> 00:35:24,330
be careful.

928
00:35:24,956 --> 00:35:26,290
I actually told Zuha too.

929
00:35:26,374 --> 00:35:27,625
About what?

930
00:35:27,708 --> 00:35:29,544
- "Hey, Zuha. It's 10:00 p.m. now."
- Right.

931
00:35:29,627 --> 00:35:30,586
Yeah. "Avoid him."

932
00:35:31,420 --> 00:35:32,296
She did tell me.

933
00:35:32,380 --> 00:35:33,756
"We're next to Boss at 10:00 p.m."

934
00:35:33,840 --> 00:35:35,216
- "Be careful."
- Right.

935
00:35:35,299 --> 00:35:37,260
I like 10:00 p.m. the most.

936
00:35:37,343 --> 00:35:38,386
Thank you for the food.

937
00:35:38,469 --> 00:35:40,012
- Thank you.
- It was so good.

938
00:35:40,096 --> 00:35:42,265
Hey, has everything
been cleaned downstairs?

939
00:35:42,765 --> 00:35:44,517
- Not yet.
- Right?

940
00:35:44,600 --> 00:35:47,687
Then, I'll clean up the kitchen.
You clean downstairs.

941
00:35:47,770 --> 00:35:48,729
Okay.

942
00:35:48,813 --> 00:35:50,273
Or someone can help me wash dishes.

943
00:35:50,356 --> 00:35:51,816
ASKING FOR HELP RIGHT AWAY

944
00:35:51,899 --> 00:35:53,276
There's a lot to clean downstairs.

945
00:35:53,359 --> 00:35:54,235
Really?

946
00:35:54,318 --> 00:35:55,695
Honestly, there is a lot.

947
00:35:55,778 --> 00:35:58,573
- Yeah, and we have to unfold the mat too.
- Right.

948
00:35:58,656 --> 00:36:00,825
- We'll come up after we're done.
- Okay.

949
00:36:03,494 --> 00:36:04,704
Come up when you're done.

950
00:36:04,787 --> 00:36:05,997
Geez, my back.

951
00:36:06,080 --> 00:36:08,332
- Let's dig deep and go clean.
- Let's do it.

952
00:36:11,377 --> 00:36:12,962
Gosh, this will take forever.

953
00:36:13,045 --> 00:36:16,549
LAST NIGHT'S PARTY AND TODAY'S LUNCH

954
00:36:25,391 --> 00:36:28,311
RUBBING THOROUGHLY

955
00:36:29,478 --> 00:36:31,230
RINSING THEM

956
00:36:31,314 --> 00:36:34,775
LIKE A SPIN DRYER

957
00:36:35,568 --> 00:36:38,571
SATISFIED

958
00:36:39,906 --> 00:36:43,117
FINISHING UP WITH CLEAN WATER

959
00:36:43,701 --> 00:36:45,870
- Let's tidy this up first.
- We should dust these off.

960
00:36:45,953 --> 00:36:46,787
- Dust them?
- Yes.

961
00:36:47,663 --> 00:36:48,623
There are so many.

962
00:36:48,706 --> 00:36:50,458
So many comforters.

963
00:36:53,419 --> 00:36:54,462
Let's do it.

964
00:36:55,713 --> 00:36:56,839
Don't drop it.

965
00:36:56,923 --> 00:36:57,965
- Ten times.
- Okay.

966
00:36:58,049 --> 00:36:58,925
Ready, set, go.

967
00:36:59,008 --> 00:37:01,844
10 TIMES IS THE OFFICIAL RULE
FOR SHAKING COMFORTERS

968
00:37:02,428 --> 00:37:04,680
Five, six, seven,

969
00:37:04,764 --> 00:37:06,974
eight, nine, ten.

970
00:37:07,058 --> 00:37:08,100
- Okay.
- All done.

971
00:37:08,184 --> 00:37:09,268
Let's go in.

972
00:37:09,352 --> 00:37:10,603
Let's go.

973
00:37:10,686 --> 00:37:11,520
There are so many.

974
00:37:11,604 --> 00:37:13,231
60 COMFORTER SHAKES LEFT

975
00:37:13,814 --> 00:37:15,399
There's an endless amount of dust.

976
00:37:19,946 --> 00:37:21,697
I think some got in my mouth.

977
00:37:21,781 --> 00:37:23,199
Bon appétit.

978
00:37:23,282 --> 00:37:24,200
Hey.

979
00:37:25,201 --> 00:37:26,661
We're almost done.

980
00:37:26,744 --> 00:37:28,412
What should we do with this?

981
00:37:29,080 --> 00:37:32,124
We can't hang it, can we?

982
00:37:32,208 --> 00:37:34,085
HANG IT HERE?

983
00:37:34,168 --> 00:37:36,629
T-SHIRT COMFORTERS WERE HUNG ON HANGERS

984
00:37:36,712 --> 00:37:38,923
BUT NOW

985
00:37:39,006 --> 00:37:41,008
ONLY 2 ARE HANGING

986
00:37:41,092 --> 00:37:42,385
You want to hang it?

987
00:37:43,052 --> 00:37:44,512
They're all going to be new guests.

988
00:37:44,595 --> 00:37:45,972
Because they're all new?

989
00:37:46,055 --> 00:37:47,098
Let's try.

990
00:37:47,181 --> 00:37:48,266
BUT…

991
00:37:48,349 --> 00:37:49,392
Will it be possible?

992
00:37:50,142 --> 00:37:54,105
THE HANGERS ARE ABOUT 3 M HIGH

993
00:37:55,147 --> 00:37:59,735
Let's give it a try and not regret it.

994
00:37:59,819 --> 00:38:01,612
- Let's do it.
- Let's do it.

995
00:38:01,696 --> 00:38:03,155
But how should we do this?

996
00:38:17,545 --> 00:38:21,257
If they made this sturdy enough,
it should be fine.

997
00:38:25,928 --> 00:38:26,762
Can you hang it?

998
00:38:26,846 --> 00:38:27,680
I can.

999
00:38:27,763 --> 00:38:28,681
SUCCESSFULLY CLIMBS UP

1000
00:38:28,764 --> 00:38:30,057
It's going to be heavy though.

1001
00:38:30,641 --> 00:38:31,934
- I'll bring it over.
- Let me see.

1002
00:38:32,018 --> 00:38:32,852
I think I can do it.

1003
00:38:32,935 --> 00:38:34,020
Okay.

1004
00:38:34,103 --> 00:38:35,438
How heavy is this?

1005
00:38:35,521 --> 00:38:37,940
I think it's about 7 kg.

1006
00:38:38,024 --> 00:38:38,858
That's insane.

1007
00:38:38,941 --> 00:38:40,067
I can do it.

1008
00:38:51,162 --> 00:38:51,996
Okay.

1009
00:38:52,872 --> 00:38:54,332
ONE IS DONE

1010
00:38:55,291 --> 00:38:56,667
Okay.

1011
00:39:01,505 --> 00:39:03,549
HANGS THE 2ND ONE IN NO TIME

1012
00:39:03,632 --> 00:39:04,842
Way to go.

1013
00:39:04,925 --> 00:39:06,093
Do the lightest ones.

1014
00:39:06,177 --> 00:39:07,678
Want to go up? I can lift you.

1015
00:39:07,762 --> 00:39:08,971
Try it.

1016
00:39:09,055 --> 00:39:10,222
- Here?
- Yeah, get on.

1017
00:39:10,306 --> 00:39:12,641
YEON-KOUNG TRIES TO LIFT
ZUHA ON HER SHOULDERS

1018
00:39:13,851 --> 00:39:16,103
Geez!

1019
00:39:16,187 --> 00:39:18,439
You must've eaten a lot of <i>ramyeon.</i>

1020
00:39:18,522 --> 00:39:19,732
- I can't go up.
- You got it?

1021
00:39:19,815 --> 00:39:20,983
- I can't.
- Why not?

1022
00:39:21,067 --> 00:39:22,318
Put your leg over the bar.

1023
00:39:22,401 --> 00:39:23,903
Wait. It's so slippery.

1024
00:39:23,986 --> 00:39:26,614
Hook your leg over the bar
and try to sit on it.

1025
00:39:27,281 --> 00:39:29,241
Hold on. Please take my sock off.

1026
00:39:29,325 --> 00:39:30,242
Your sock?

1027
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:33,579
Damn it, where is it?

1028
00:39:33,662 --> 00:39:34,497
One, two, three.

1029
00:39:36,457 --> 00:39:37,583
Yes, that's it.

1030
00:39:41,337 --> 00:39:42,505
Oh, my gosh. Can you make it?

1031
00:39:42,588 --> 00:39:43,589
Okay!

1032
00:39:45,508 --> 00:39:47,009
- You got it.
- I got it!

1033
00:39:47,093 --> 00:39:48,260
- We did it.
- We got it.

1034
00:39:48,344 --> 00:39:49,929
- I'm seated.
- We did it.

1035
00:39:50,012 --> 00:39:51,639
The first step's done.

1036
00:39:51,722 --> 00:39:53,140
Now, you have to stand up.

1037
00:39:53,224 --> 00:39:54,683
You have to stand up.

1038
00:39:54,767 --> 00:39:55,643
Stand up.

1039
00:39:55,726 --> 00:39:58,396
CAN'T HELP BUT LAUGH

1040
00:39:58,479 --> 00:39:59,313
MOPPING

1041
00:39:59,397 --> 00:40:00,856
How did you get up there?

1042
00:40:00,940 --> 00:40:02,483
I lifted her up on my shoulders.

1043
00:40:02,566 --> 00:40:03,567
Be careful.

1044
00:40:04,568 --> 00:40:05,403
- That's it.
- Careful.

1045
00:40:05,486 --> 00:40:06,362
I can do this, right?

1046
00:40:07,405 --> 00:40:08,614
Okay, I'm up.

1047
00:40:08,697 --> 00:40:10,116
I'll bring a comforter.

1048
00:40:10,991 --> 00:40:12,284
You wanted to do this.

1049
00:40:12,368 --> 00:40:13,911
- I did?
- Yes.

1050
00:40:13,994 --> 00:40:14,829
RIGHT, I DID

1051
00:40:14,912 --> 00:40:15,913
Oh, no.

1052
00:40:20,084 --> 00:40:21,377
How did they hang these?

1053
00:40:21,460 --> 00:40:22,670
Hold on a second.

1054
00:40:23,921 --> 00:40:25,089
RIGHT IN

1055
00:40:25,172 --> 00:40:26,340
There you go.

1056
00:40:26,424 --> 00:40:27,550
- Very good.
- All right.

1057
